# Unity development workflow

## Project layout

- Unity project root: `unity/`
- Agent skills (project-local): `unity/.cursor/skills/` (`unity-cli`, `unity-pipeline`)
- Official Unity skill pack (user-global): `~/.cursor/skills/` from `~/.cursor/unity-agent-plugin`
- Pipeline HTTP fallback: `unity/Tools/Invoke-UnityPipeline.ps1`

## Stack

- Unity **6000.6.x** (6.6), template **Universal 2D** (URP 2D Renderer)
- Drive the live Editor with the **official Unity CLI** and **official `unity mcp`** (Pipeline). Do not use Coplay / `MCPForUnity` / `localhost:8080/mcp`.
- Prefer live Editor commands (`unity command`, `unity command eval`, or Unity MCP tools) over hand-editing `.unity` YAML when Pipeline is connected (`unity status` → ready).
- Domain how-to comes from Unity's official skills (`unity-cli`, `unity-pipeline`, UI/2D/URP/package skills). Keep them current with `unity skill refresh` and `git -C $env:USERPROFILE\.cursor\unity-agent-plugin pull`.

## CLI / MCP habits

```powershell
cd F:\Gdev\Repos\GearDefenders\unity
unity status --project-path F:\Gdev\Repos\GearDefenders\unity
unity open . --args "-automated"   # preferred: avoids modal dialog stalls
unity command set_autotick --enable true   # keep Editor ticking while unfocused
```

Project MCP config lives at [`.cursor/mcp.json`](../mcp.json) and launches `unity mcp --project-path <this unity project>`. After changing it, reload Cursor MCP. This project pins `com.unity.pipeline` **0.7.0-exp.1**; drive the Editor with `unity command` / `unity command eval`. If the CLI cannot parse command lines, fall back to [`unity/Tools/Invoke-UnityPipeline.ps1`](unity/Tools/Invoke-UnityPipeline.ps1).
